Release	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-01T14:58:21.9466352Z [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/2396","id":4703334188,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABGFcvLA","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2396","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2396.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2396.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2396","number":2396,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: make the repeated-tool-call breaker opt-in and never auto-merge without the issue link (#2395)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #2395\n\nThe repeated-tool-call breaker (#2247, #2316) was always on and stopped a session after 3 identical failing calls. `gh pr checks` exits with code 8 while checks are pending ([documented](https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_pr_checks)), so three ordinary CI polls killed Codex sessions that were only waiting for CI. This happened in [link-assistant/agent#323](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/323#issuecomment-5896427734) and [konard/p-vs-np#623](https://github.com/konard/p-vs-np/pull/623#issuecomment-5897797370).\n\nIn p-vs-np#623, the description was rewritten at 20:10:37 without `Fixes #567`, and the auto-merge merged it at 20:11:31 without checking again. Issue #567 stayed open. The log attached at 20:08:58 did not cover the merge.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **The breaker is opt-in, with a default limit of 10** (`--detect-repeated-tool-calls` / `HIVE_MIND_DETECT_REPEATED_TOOL_CALLS=true`, `--repeated-tool-call-limit` default 10, was 3).\n   - CI polling (`gh pr checks`, `gh run view/list/watch`, `gh pr view … statusCheckRollup`, `gh api …/check-runs`, `sleep`, `--watch`, …) is never counted, even when the breaker is enabled.\n   - Failing calls only count as repeated when their output repeats too.\n   - Applies to every tool: claude, codex, opencode, agent, gemini and qwen. CONFIGURATION docs are updated in all languages.\n2. **A breaker stop no longer ends the auto-merge.** The restart-until-mergeable loop attaches the stopped session's log and continues with feedback instead of reporting \"🚨 Solution Draft Failed / 🛑 Automation stopped\" (`src/solve.auto-merge-session-stop.lib.mjs`).\n3. **The issue link is ensured right before every auto-merge.**\n   - New `src/pr-issue-link-merge-gate.lib.mjs`, used by both `solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs` and `solve.auto-merge-attempt.lib.mjs` immediately before `mergePullRequest`.\n   - A missing `Fixes #N` is restored before the merge.\n   - If the description cannot be read or written, the merge is held back (`issue_link_unverified`), and the \"auto-merge blocked\" comment explains how to fix the description.\n4. **The full log is attached again when the auto-merge is held back** (`attachLogAfterAutoMergeBlocked`). This is in addition to the #2306 re-upload after restart loops.\n5. **Verbose diagnostic for the unknown 20:10:37 editor.**\n   - With `--verbose`, every finished AI session (the first session and each restart iteration) logs the processes still running in its work directory (`src/session-survivors.lib.mjs`).\n   - Codex runs tool commands under `setsid()`, so they can outlive the killed process group.\n   - Nothing is killed automatically, so legitimate work is never interfered with.\n\n### Case study\n\n[`docs/case-studies/issue-2395/README.md`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/issue-2395-559adda5fe3c/docs/case-studies/issue-2395/README.md) contains:\n\n- the timeline of both incidents,\n- every requirement and its status,\n- root causes RC1–RC5,\n- online facts with sources (gh exit codes, the Codex `setsid` design, command-stream kill semantics),\n- the decision on upstream issues (none filed: all upstream behaviour is documented or intentional, and there is no reproducible defect yet),\n- the remaining uncertainty.\n\nThe raw data is included: both full logs, with the account email and id redacted, plus the PR, comment, edit-history and timeline JSON.\n\n### How to reproduce\n\n```\nnode experiments/replay-gh-pr-checks-polling-2395.mjs /path/to/v2.33.2/src   # TRIPPED on poll 3 (both runs)\nnode experiments/replay-gh-pr-checks-polling-2395.mjs                        # not tripped\n```\n\nThe replay feeds the exact `gh pr checks` records from both logs (`tests/fixtures/issue-2395-*-gh-pr-checks.jsonl`) through the guard.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `tests/repeated-tool-call-opt-in-2395.test.mjs` (14) covers:\n  - off by default for every tool,\n  - the default limit of 10,\n  - polling exemption with the real fixtures,\n  - output-sensitive counting,\n  - auto-merge continuing with feedback and attaching the stopped session's log.\n- `tests/pr-issue-link-before-merge-2395.test.mjs` (13) covers:\n  - the gate restoring `Fixes #567` on the exact merged description,\n  - fail-closed on read, write and throw errors,\n  - both merge paths wired,\n  - the blocked comment,\n  - the log re-attach on a held-back merge.\n- `tests/session-survivors-2395.test.mjs` (7) covers:\n  - finding a detached process left in the work directory,\n  - verbose-only behaviour,\n  - logging format,\n  - wiring into every session.\n- Updated: `tests/claude-repeated-tool-call-breaker-2247.test.mjs`, `tests/repeated-tool-call-all-tools-2316.test.mjs`, `tests/test-closed-issue-merge-blocking-2144.mjs`.\n\nLocally, all of these pass:\n\n- `npm test` (523 test files),\n- `npm run lint`,\n- `npm run format:check`,\n- `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`,\n- `secretlint`.\n\n### CI note: freshness gate and npm audit\n\n\"Checks and release\" stopped at `detect-changes` (`Dependency freshness failed: 10 stale`, run 36867760075), and \"Security\" failed on `npm audit` (run 36867759543). Both came from upstream changes, not from this PR. CI must pass, so they are fixed here in two separate commits:\n\n1. **Gate fix (root cause): `scripts/dependency-freshness.lib.mjs`.** The gate checked `FROM rust:1.98-slim-bookworm` against rust-lang/rust GitHub tags. rust-lang tagged 1.99.0 at 12:41Z, 38 minutes before the run. Docker Hub had not published any `rust:1.99*` image yet, so the only way to pass the gate was a `FROM` line that cannot be pulled. The rust pin is now a `docker` record resolved by `resolveDockerHubLatest('library/rust')`, which returns the newest stable `X.Y.Z` tag the registry actually serves. If the registry returns no versions, the check fails rather than passing. Tests are in `tests/dependency-freshness-2264.test.mjs` and fail without the fix.\n2. **Pin refresh.** `@link-assistant/agent` 0.26.8 → 0.26.11 (`Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dind`), `@sentry/node` and `@sentry/profiling-node` ^11.1.0 → ^11.2.0, `jscpd` ^5.3.3 → ^5.4.0, use-m `@dotenvx/dotenvx` 2.31.1 → 2.32.3. In the lockfile, `brace-expansion` 5.0.9 → 5.0.12 (GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr, GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7, GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p). The pin tests are updated to match.\n\nLocally: `node scripts/check-dependency-freshness.mjs` reports 151/151 declarations current, `npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high` finds 0 vulnerabilities, and `npm test` passes all 523 test files. Lint, format and duplication checks also pass.\n\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:start -->\n### Changes\n- 61 file(s) modified\n- 1366 line(s) added\n- 243 line(s) removed\n- Files:\n  - `.changeset/opt-in-repeated-tool-call-breaker.md`\n  - `.gitattributes`\n  - `Dockerfile`\n  - `Dockerfile.dind`\n  - `docs/CONFIGURATION.hi.md`\n  - `docs/CONFIGURATION.md`\n  - `docs/CONFIGURATION.ru.md`\n  - `docs/CONFIGURATION.zh.md`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/README.md`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/agent-pr323-comment-5896427734.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/agent-pr323-comment-5896435509.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/agent-pr323-comment-5896436158.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/agent-pr323.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/hive-mind-issue-2395.md`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/hive-mind-log-N8APcJ-sanitized.log.txt.gz`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/hive-mind-log-wv1oqj-sanitized.log.txt.gz`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623-comment-5897797370.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623-comment-5897808960.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623-comments.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623-edits.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623-timeline.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/raw/p-vs-np-pr623.json`\n  - `docs/case-studies/issue-2395/replay-gh-pr-checks-polling.txt`\n  - `experiments/replay-gh-pr-checks-polling-2395.mjs`\n  - `package-lock.json`\n  - `package.json`\n  - `scripts/dependency-freshness.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/agent.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/attach-logs-guarantee.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/automation-stop-reporting.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/claude.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/codex.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/gemini.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/opencode.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/pr-issue-link-merge-gate.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/qwen.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/repeated-tool-call-breaker.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/session-result.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/session-survivors.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.auto-merge-attempt.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.auto-merge-session-stop.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.config.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.mjs`\n  - `src/solve.restart-shared.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/tool-call-loop-guard.lib.mjs`\n  - `src/use-with-retry.lib.mjs`\n  - `tests/claude-repeated-tool-call-breaker-2247.test.mjs`\n  - `tests/dependency-freshness-2264.test.mjs`\n  - `tests/fixtures/issue-2395-agent-gh-pr-checks.jsonl`\n  - …and 11 more\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:end -->\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:00:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T14:46:04Z","closed_at":"2026-10-01T14:46:04Z","merged_at":"2026-10-01T14:46:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"ce6ff78401a325615cd9cc809b258b5ee9fdac79","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/2396/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/2396/comments","review_comme